from __future__ import annotations
BOARD_CITATION_CONTRACT = "\nCitation contract for the board document. Whenever a passage you write takes its substance from\nmaterial supplied for this turn — an uploaded document or book, a code repository, a linked page,\npasted text, a transcript, or any other external material in the payload — that passage carries a\ncitation, exactly as a published work does.\n\nWrite the inline marker as `[^1]` at the end of the sentence or passage it supports, after the\nsentence punctuation. Put several markers in a row when one passage rests on several references.\nMarkers belong in ordinary body text, and never inside a heading, code fence, formula, table\ndelimiter, or a placeholder owned by OpenClass.\n\nWrite one reference entry per cited location at the very end of the document, each on a single line\nof its own, as `[^1]: ...`, under a short reference heading written in the document's language. An\nentry names the work and the exact location inside it — the title, plus whichever of chapter or\nsection, page range, repository path with line range, timestamp, or address applies — so that a\nreader can reach the same passage. Write entries in the document's language. Never put an internal\nidentifier such as an evidence ID, chunk ID, ingestion ID, or platform file path in an entry.\n\nWhen supplied evidence has `citation_number` or `citation_numbers`, these numbers identify exact\nsource locations. Copy the assigned number for each location into both its marker and definition.\nDo not replace supplied numbers with your own sequence, and do not use an attachment's array index\nas its citation number. For example, if the locations you use have assigned numbers 2, 4, and 9,\nwrite `[^2]`, `[^4]`, and `[^9]`; OpenClass will renumber the finished document while preserving\nthose exact evidence identities. The title and location in each definition must describe the\nevidence assigned to that number. If a required location has no supplied number, do not invent a\nnumber or bind it to another location; report the missing evidence.\n\nOnly when the material has no supplied citation-number map, number markers in ascending order of\nfirst appearance, starting at 1. Every marker has exactly one entry, and every entry is cited by at\nleast one marker. Cite only material actually supplied for\nthis turn, and only the location you actually used: never invent a work, a page, or a line range,\nand never cite material you were not given. Do not cite your own general knowledge, your own worked\nexamples, or content the learner wrote in the conversation.\n\nWhen you edit a document that already carries a reference list, keep the existing pairs intact.\nReuse the number already listed for a location instead of adding a second entry for it, add entries\nfor newly used locations, and remove an entry once the passage that cited it is gone. Keep the\nreference list last in the document. OpenClass renumbers the pairs after your turn. Preserve the\nsupplied evidence numbers until that backend step; marker, definition, and evidence must agree.\n".strip()
